  concept: "Authored objective: Sustained backup power.\nAuthored requirement: LED
    current at least 2 mA for 2 accepted simulated seconds, capacitor drops at least
    0.20 V. current \u2265 2 mA. Conduction required.\nGeneral teaching principle:
    Electrical measurements are differences or flows that require a correct reference,
    operating condition and fresh solver evidence.\nOnly fresh, authoritative game
    evidence can establish that this objective is complete."
  analogy: A pressure gauge needs a reference; a voltage measurement likewise depends
    on its defined points.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: An expected rail or current is not a measured rail or current until
    the live circuit evidence confirms it.
  baseline: "Before working on \u2018Sustained backup power\u2019, which component,
    reference or condition mentioned in the authored requirement should you inspect
    first? Explain your reasoning."
  prediction: "For \u2018Sustained backup power\u2019, what result or observation
    would you expect if the required setup is correct? Distinguish a predicted result
    from a measured result."
  practice: "In Level 29, perform the objective \u2018Sustained backup power\u2019
    in the actual game laboratory. Compare fresh evidence against: LED current at
    least 2 mA for 2 accepted simulated seconds, capacitor drops at least 0.20 V.
    current \u2265 2 mA. Conduction required.\nThe mission evaluator decides completion;
    this tutorial does not grade your answer."
